            "review_text": "IamMissAshley\n4 contributions\n0\nPrices are EXPENSIVE!!!\nJan 2017 • Friends\nWell, the food is good, I'd give it 4.5 stars. But, the service is so-so. I went to have dinner with a friend, we didn't order a lot of food, but the final bill was 1.3M+ dong (equivalent to SGD$80+). I eat lots of hotpot in Singapore, some of them are the best, and I have never had such a bill for 2 person before. The price is way over the top considering that this is in Vietnam! The killer is the soup, which cost 268,000 dong (SGD$17) for 2 types of soup! Furthermore, it is just a normal restaurant, nothing fancy. I will definitely NOT go there again, unless there is nothing else to eat in hcmc!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 30, 2017",
